From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: keep the vsync interrupt of an idle video mode
 encoder

Until "drm/msm/dpu: count the pending frame before kicking it off" the
frame_pending count of a CRTC stayed one too high, so a video mode
encoder never reached DPU_ENC_RC_STATE_IDLE. With the count fixed, an
idle desktop enters the idle state IDLE_TIMEOUT (58 ms) after every
frame done: the vsync and underrun interrupts are unregistered, and the
next kickoff registers them again - many times a second, a path video
mode encoders had not run on this tablet before.

On the OnePlus Pad 4 (Kaanapali, a dual-DSI video mode panel with DSC)
mid-session display stalls appeared with exactly that change: two
"vblank timeout: 400000" / "wait for commit done returned -110" pairs
about 60 ms apart, i.e. the commit's own wait and the next commit's
wait for the previous flush, each 50 ms with only the DSC flush bit
(CTL_FLUSH bit 22) still pending. Boots of the kernels before it showed
none. The mechanism is not known yet.

Keep video mode encoders in DPU_ENC_RC_STATE_ON after a frame done, as
before the count was fixed, unless the new module parameter
msm.dpu_vid_idle_irq_off (0644, default off) asks for the idle state;
the corrected frame_pending accounting itself stays. The parameter is
read at every frame done, so the two behaviours can be compared at run
time.

Also print the INTF timing engine state (enabled, frame and line count)
and the vblank reference count with a vblank timeout: a stuck flush on
a running INTF then reads differently from a stopped INTF.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c   | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c  | 12 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 93ad4248930c..14df37deeb2e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -344,6 +344,16 @@ module_param_cb(dpu_idle_refresh_hz, &dpu_idle_rr_param_ops,
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dpu_idle_refresh_hz,
 		 "Lowest idle refresh rate: the slowest panel rate at or above it that differs from the mode only in the vertical front porch (default 60)");
 
+/*
+ * An idle video mode encoder (no frame for IDLE_TIMEOUT) used to drop its
+ * vsync interrupt until the next kickoff. Keep it on unless this is set, see
+ * the DPU_ENC_RC_EVENT_FRAME_DONE case of dpu_encoder_resource_control().
+ */
+static bool dpu_vid_idle_irq_off;
+module_param(dpu_vid_idle_irq_off, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dpu_vid_idle_irq_off,
+		 "Drop the vsync interrupt of an idle video mode encoder until the next commit (default: keep it on)");
+
 /* @b differs from @a at most in the length of the vertical front porch */
 static bool dpu_idle_rr_same_but_vfp(const struct drm_display_mode *a,
 				     const struct drm_display_mode *b)
@@ -1622,6 +1632,16 @@ static int dpu_encoder_resource_control(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc,
 			return 0;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * A video mode encoder only drops its vsync interrupt in the
+		 * idle state. Until the frame_pending count was fixed it never
+		 * got there; now an idle desktop enters and leaves it many
+		 * times a second, and the CTL flush timeouts of a dual-DSI
+		 * panel came with that. Stay on unless asked otherwise.
+		 */
+		if (is_vid_mode && !READ_ONCE(dpu_vid_idle_irq_off))
+			return 0;
+
 		queue_delayed_work(priv->kms->wq, &dpu_enc->delayed_off_work,
 				   msecs_to_jiffies(dpu_enc->idle_timeout));
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
index 9ddae7581d0d..bffe55bc20f2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -586,7 +586,17 @@ static int dpu_encoder_phys_vid_wait_for_commit_done(
 		(hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl) == 0),
 		msecs_to_jiffies(50));
 	if (ret <= 0) {
-		DPU_ERROR("vblank timeout: %x\n", hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl));
+		struct dpu_hw_intf_status s = {0};
+
+		if (phys_enc->hw_intf && phys_enc->hw_intf->ops.get_status)
+			phys_enc->hw_intf->ops.get_status(phys_enc->hw_intf, &s);
+
+		/* the timing engine state tells a stuck flush from a stopped INTF */
+		DPU_ERROR("vblank timeout: %x, intf %d en %u frame %u line %u, vblank refs %d\n",
+			  hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl),
+			  phys_enc->hw_intf ? phys_enc->hw_intf->idx - INTF_0 : -1,
+			  s.is_en, s.frame_count, s.line_count,
+			  READ_ONCE(phys_enc->vblank_refcount));
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
 
